{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1489162-new-character-ithaeur-advice","id":1489162,"title":"New Character/Ithaeur Advice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-04T16:03:20-07:00","id":1489162,"title":"New Character/Ithaeur Advice","content":"Hi all, I had posted a similar topic about playing my first Vampire in the Requiem forums and got such great advice that I thought I would try the same with my first attempt at Forsaken. I played Apocalypse a lot back in the day but after reading the core, this is a very different animal. I'll be making an Ithaeur and I was wondering if there were some things that I should avoid or make sure I get stat wise. Sometimes things look good on paper but don't play out practically that way, after all. For instance, are there any Gifts or Rites that are must haves to properly fill the role. He isn't an overly physical character but this is werewolf, so how much Brawl should I safely have? Some of the new morality components are great but I was having trouble with the Breaking Points to be created. Any help is appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27502-caelican","name":"Caelican","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T18:24:47-07:00","id":1489174,"title":"","content":"A single dot of Brawl to keep you out of unSkilled penalties and let you effectively use your natural weapons is a solid baseline, while two dots will suffice for base competency in a fight.<br /> <br /> A lot of other build advice is going to depend on the character's tribe, given its impact on starting Renown and Gift affinities, as well as how you plan to specialize their role as a Spirit Master; if this character going to be mostly acting as a scout and/or intelligence-gatherer, that's going to be a different beast than if you plan to act as a sorcerous siege engine, which in turn requires a different focus than if you intend to perform rites to better maintain the pack's territory.<br /> <br /> If the multiple Merits whose effects are explicitly specialization-oriented trade-offs didn't tip you off, Werewolf characters do well by having a niche in the larger dynamic of the pack. What are you hoping to cover for your fellow players (current or hypothetical)?<br /> <br /> Optimization-wise, starting with one dot in Wisdom means you start with a Wolf Gift instead of the second dot in the Crescent Moon's Gift, and you can unlock a Wolf Gift Facet you have the Renown for at any time for the price of a one-dot Merit; between that and the fact that you only start with two Shadow Gift Facets, there's relatively little reason to spread out your starting Renown further than a 2/1 split.<br /> <br /> If you don't plan on leading the Siskur-Dah for the pack (or providing a tribal benefit to that rite that you anticipate the pack will need), it may be prudent to take a different rite or rites with your free dots, depending on your intended role.<br /> <br /> Think of it like creating a member of a heist crew: is your Ithaeur the hacker, the lookout, the guy who's highly knowledgeable about the specific sorts of things the crew is going after? Being primed to deal with spirits is a starting point from which the rest of the build needs a direction to go in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T18:41:20-07:00","id":1489175,"title":"","content":"I think build wise he's suited as the &quot;brains&quot; or researcher role for a pack. There is definitely an investigative component to that as well. Character wise, I'd like to see him interacting heavily with spirits. My CoD background is with Mage so something that veers towards as close to Werewolf has to Merlin would be good. Lots of dealing with spirits in a negotiating fashion or compelling if that falls through. He is going to be Iron Master so there is a Cunning side to all of it. Maybe not being tricky so much as good at planning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27502-caelican","name":"Caelican","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T21:29:08-07:00","id":1489183,"title":"","content":"For research you will absolutely want Sift the Sands, which <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/491309-your-werewolf-starter-kit-2e-facet-baselines?p=491418#post491418\">any Iron Master Ithaeur can pick as a starting Facet without any special Renown investment</a>. There are unfortunately not many other Shadow Gifts in the starting kit that specifically help with research or spirits without going into a third Renown category, so your second pick may be best chosen with an eye toward being able to unlock more Facets without needing to spend Experiences opening up the Gift first; Iron Slave or Garble will give you the in on Technology to get at Command Artifice, or you could try and put Moldywarp or Sculpt to use in hiding out or preparing things for spirits and/or prey with particular needs. The overlap in affinities slightly limits your starting options, which may shift your early-game priorities toward getting stuff like the Gift of Warding, Evasion, or Insight for tricks like Prey on Weakness, Read the World's Loom, One Step Ahead, Deny Everything, Exit Strategy, Ward the Wolf's Den, and Boundary Ward.<br /> <br /> Wolf Gifts to pick up include Honed Senses, Impossible Spoor, Reflected Facets, and Pack Awareness. The Crescent Moon's Gift readily provides tools for dealing with spirits and gathering information, and starting with the second dot will open up another avenue of information-gathering even without active spirits to question.<br /> <br /> Hunting Ground will provide social benefits that also apply to spirits at the cost of upkeep activity a healthy pack should be engaging in anyway as an alternative to learning Sacred Hunt, or if you can spare an extra Merit dot (or three, depending on how your ST arbitrates the steps of character creation) then Supplication will make negotiations with your choice of spirit type easier at the cost of a Ban Condition that you can leverage for Beats. Starting with a couple of extra rites should help the character concept get more done early on to compensate for the relative lack of starting Gift options, though entirely burning your starting Merit dots on them is probably inadvisable; Messenger, Shadowbind, and/or Shadowcall should suffice, with Totemic Empowerment potentially also useful with the right sort of totem and Wellspring likewise with the right sort of locus. Like with the Gift options, it may be prudent to put picking up more options from spirits through Sacred Hunts on the short list of things to do in the early game.<br /> <br /> Speaking of loci, Dedicated Locus is just generally useful for a pack to have access to, and gaining the Merit's mechanical benefit individually requires an investment of at least one dot, but if you don't need to spend a lot of Essence at once and the rest of the players are okay with it you can rely on them to foot the bill for the starting dots and the required Safe Place. If you've got two dots of Wisdom then Resonance Shaper will synergize well with access to a locus, which in turn will help with spiritual negotiations.<br /> <br /> Moon-Kissed on an Ithaeur can outright give you persistent 9-Again on Animal Ken, Medicine, or Occult as long as you're willing to lose 10-Again on another Skill. Residential Area gives you a moderately versatile source of temporary Social Merits in a way that's right up the Iron Masters' alley, though it's less useful if you're looking to interact with spirits and haven't cultivated a particular sort of human herd.<br /> <br /> Basically, the big point of difficulty is going to be prioritizing your starting Merit dots between Merits and Rites and finding time to expand your portfolio. The good news is, if you can get a good run of Sacred Hunts going you can probably earn some extra Renown in the process, which should make picking up new tools go quicker, and even without that, Bans are good for getting into trouble that gives you Beats. Working out the particulars with your fellow players is advisable to balance character focuses in a way everyone can be satisfied with, but as far as starting builds go from here it's going to come down to taste and setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T21:42:40-07:00","id":1489185,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all that! Since the created Breaking Points factor in Auspice, what are some of the options that fit with Ithaeur but are not too hamstringing. For a Toward Spirit I was probably going to go with something Pack based like: Abandoning a Pack Member to Danger. The Toward Flesh maybe something like: Forcing a Spirit to do your Bidding. But that seems limiting to the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27502-caelican","name":"Caelican","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T22:10:41-07:00","id":1489186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caelican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1489162-new-character-ithaeur-advice?p=1489185#post1489185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for all that! Since the created Breaking Points factor in Auspice, what are some of the options that fit with Ithaeur but are not too hamstringing. For a Toward Spirit I was probably going to go with something Pack based like: Abandoning a Pack Member to Danger. The Toward Flesh maybe something like: Forcing a Spirit to do your Bidding. But that seems limiting to the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspice, tribe, and Touchstones, to be precise. I'd look at the &quot;Making A Hunter&quot; section on page 28 and the tribe writeup on pages 43-45, as well as thinking about the character's physical and spiritual Touchstones, to come up with some specific incidents that would shift the character's balance in one direction or the other, then generalize outward from those as needed.<br /> <br /> The point is less to come up with a tribal vow-level add-on to the list than it is to personalize ways the character's Harmony can waver; to give a loose comparison for another gameline, it's like how Demon asks you five questions that don't create new conditions for compromising Cover so much as they elaborate on characters that might cause your character to suffer compromise in interesting ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T18:46:44-07:00","id":1490206,"title":"","content":"Very possible I just missed this but in trying to pick stats, what is the usual role to try to detect what the resonance of a location is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27502-caelican","name":"Caelican","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T19:14:30-07:00","id":1490207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caelican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1489162-new-character-ithaeur-advice?p=1490206#post1490206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very possible I just missed this but in trying to pick stats, what is the usual role to try to detect what the resonance of a location is?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way the Hisil reflects resonance means it's going to generally be fairly obvious, particularly once you get a look at the type of spirits that occupy the area, but Occult and Wits or Intelligence should suffice to connect the dots if a roll is needed for a particularly obscure or complex form of resonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}